; An offload pointer: the compact stand-in a tool returns instead of a 50KB blob.
; It is an ordinary record. The `(! data/offload …)` spelling it used to carry is
; a protocol FRAME, and `!` is not a character Core §2 produces; the payload is
; ASN and the frame around it is docs/AGENTIC_PROTOCOL.md's business.
;
; canonical: (:offload "scrape-9481" :summary "Extracted 42 product items. Status 200. Zero parse errors." :size-bytes 54200 :sample [(:sku "A1" :price 24.50) (:sku "A2" :price 12.00)])

(:offload "scrape-9481"
 :summary "Extracted 42 product items. Status 200. Zero parse errors."
 :size-bytes 54200
 :sample [(:sku "A1" :price 24.50)
          (:sku "A2" :price 12.00)])
